KG42.register("clusters-a0040c1fc9491c71e3c09a0f",{"id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v142-d-K003","paper":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets","label":"Constrained contract selection, bilateral price adjustment and day-ahead allocation pricing","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Constrained contract selection, bilateral price adjustment and day-ahead allocation pricing","market_meaning":"Under the negotiable trading network, pre-entry resource plans and constraints of various entities, agents select contract portfolios and iteratively adjust prices according to differences in buyer and seller choices until prices no longer change. Candidate results include local contract allocations and per-contract prices; stability, efficiency and DSO demand feasibility retain their respective source conditions, and the current mathematical interface is not yet closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["participation","matching","clearing","coordination","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The core scope is day-ahead negotiation of the same mechanism. A stable result requires fully substitutable preferences, the local improvement procedure requires the single-step improvement property, and satisfaction of DSO demand further requires sufficient resource flexibility. The per-period balancing of aggregators without their own resources and the substitution constraints when they have their own resources are retained as conditional branches. R004 provides only baseline or applicable direct-trading permissions, and its near-real-time extension is not included in this cluster's execution conclusion; R005 provides only the entry-plan interface.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Contract selection generates price-adjustment feedback, bids determine the contracts selectable in the next round, and the stopping condition is linked to the final allocation and prices; therefore the three core chains jointly express one negotiated allocation rule. Participation and matching only share their source-supported input interfaces; payment obligations are placed in a separate cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides individual choices, resource and demand constraints, and conditions for result feasibility and stability."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the bilateral bid states, excess-demand feedback, price-adjustment branches and stopping condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the interpretation of per-unit pricing and the final contract price; constraints duplicated with clearing and coordination are retained as mappings and are not counted as independent rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only references the pre-entry plan as the source of fixed resource plans in clearing; does not change the entire participation chain into a clearing dependency."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only references the applicable counterparty permissions to delimit the potential trading network; does not introduce a not-yet-implemented near-real-time branch."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Pf-it","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E25"],"rationale":"The source explicitly brings the pre-entry retail resource plan into the flexibility market. This plan can be optimized in prior scheduling and serves as a fixed input in R002; this interface does not merge the local roles of the two stages."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The source places potential contracts between tradable entity pairs and determines potential transactions and initializes prices at the start of bargaining. Permissions therefore delimit the negotiation counterparties, but C does not explicitly give a construction formula from permissions to the transaction set."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Xi","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"],"rationale":"Each round's bids are used to construct the upstream and downstream contracts selectable by agents, which are then selected according to individual utility. This is an interface from bids to selection input, not an identity mapping between price quantities and contract sets."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime-i","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X006","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The supplied excerpt divides selection results into upstream and downstream contracts and then identifies transactions selected by buyers but not selected by sellers. The overall selection, side-specific selections and excess-demand set have different roles and cannot be directly declared to be the same quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The excerpt interprets the aggregation of upstream selections at stopping as the market result and explains stability under fully substitutable preferences. This source supports functional linkage, but C has not yet expressed the complete mapping from terminal selections to the global result."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e25"],"rationale":"The DSO continuously raises bids for unrealized and necessary contracts, which links to the terminal allocation satisfying the demand boundary; this result is explicitly conditional on sufficient prosumer flexibility and cannot be generalized into an unconditional feasibility guarantee."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The two chains respectively reference the buyer and seller bid states of the same mechanism in the update and pricing interpretations. Bid sides always remain separate; equality of the two sides' prices is not inferred from the stopping condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"rationale":"The two records express the restriction, within the same result set, that each transaction corresponds to at most one contract; the pricing chain emphasizes its unique-price meaning and does not constitute an additional independent rule."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"Both reference the same stopping condition of no price change, but R003 records completion determination, while R006 also claims that an agreed price is reached. Retain the different expressions; do not treat the stopping predicate as a complete proof of price consistency."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The same frozen node appears in contract selection and its price-adjustment feedback, both referring to the local allocation activity of this mechanism. Only a display representative is selected; the original references are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"All three references belong to the same iterative price-coordination process. The node may share a display representative, but the existing edges with different directions in R002 and R003 are not thereby regarded as duplicate edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The common source and definition indicate that both are buyer bids for the same transaction and the same round; R003 explicitly marks the round, and R006 retains the round in the index. Both local records are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"Both represent seller bids for the same transaction and the same round, serving respectively the update and pricing interpretations; they are not merged with buyer bids."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"Both reference the final feasible contract result of the same local market, not a temporary selection in an arbitrary round. The design_selection of R002 and the operational annotation of R006 are retained as local roles and are not rewritten as a single object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O006","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"rationale":"The two set formulations have the same applicable objects and per-transaction contract-count restriction. The unique-price interpretation of R006 remains accessible; representative selection is for display only and does not delete any original constraint."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O007","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The same stopping condition is recorded respectively as a completion determination and as a price-result condition, but the two complete statements are not equivalent. The association as alternative expressions of the stopping condition is retained, and no unified representative is selected."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G006","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R003's excess-demand expression uses the transaction ID to test membership in the set of contract tuples selected by sellers, while the buyer membership test uses contract prices that are not explicitly tied to a bid side. If executed directly according to the listed set types, it is impossible to reliably judge whether the seller selected the same transaction.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the transaction IDs, contract tuples and bid notation in the original text, and have the upstream clarify the object types of the membership tests and the price correspondences; this round retains the original formulas and does not correct them on its own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R002's per-period contract objects are defined by the available set, yet the constraints are applied to the selected portfolio; they lack an explicit projection relation to R003's upstream and downstream selections with rounds. The mapping from terminal selections to the global result, the per-round available sets, and the state preservation of unadjusted components are also not fully expressed in C.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Xi","v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime","v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime-i","v141-c-R002::x::x-Yit","v141-c-R002::x::x-Zit","v141-c-R002::x::x-Ydt","v141-c-R002::x::x-Zdt","v141-c-R002::x::x-Yjt","v141-c-R002::x::x-Zjt","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should distinguish available sets, candidate selections, per-period subsets and final results, and supplement the source-supported round interface and complete state updates; these different sets must not be directly mapped to the same quantity."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"upstream_missing","description":"theta-Ui only points to the utility definitions of various entity types, and current C does not preserve their complete expressions, the definition of full substitutability, or their verification content. Feasibility constraints and a stopping condition alone cannot independently close the stability and Pareto-efficiency arguments; arbitrary alternative utilities or resource extensions also cannot automatically inherit the guarantees.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Ui","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C009","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e19"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-agent-utility-choice","proposal:v141-b-g01-stable-outcome","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"The upstream should supplement and verify the referential closure among utility, applicable conditions and guarantees, and confirm the correspondence between the entity names in the theorem excerpts and the utility objects; retain the substitutive relation between the aggregator baseline and the resource extension, without imposing both sets of conditions simultaneously."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The selection correspondence is defined via argmax as a set-valued object, but the stability and upstream/downstream extraction notation again seems to operate on one already selected portfolio. The local improvement procedure also lacks an in-C expression of the adjustment object and feasible initialization; one cannot conclude merely from the existing process sentences that an executable algorithm has been closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C011","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e28"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-agent-utility-choice"],"required_work":"Check the source notation for the selection correspondence and the selected portfolio, clarify the semantics of each expression when there are multiple optima, and have the upstream supplement the source-defined local adjustment and feasibility treatment; do not set a selection strategy on one's own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R006-C001 only expresses that the bids on each side remain unchanged between adjacent rounds; it does not express equality of the two sides' bids or how the jointly agreed contract price is determined. Therefore the stopping condition and per-contract uniqueness are still insufficient to close bilateral price formation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the mechanism corresponding the two sides' selections at termination to the contract price, and have the upstream supplement or delimit its expression; cross-round invariance must not be used to replace consistency between buyer and seller prices."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G011","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The current excerpt of Eq. (4) differs regarding the storage lower bound and time index; the unit relationship between DSO demand quantity and contract count is also not clarified in C. Δp carries the case's bid unit and numerical range and cannot directly serve as a universal monetary increment for all scenarios.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-E-lower","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-PD-t","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e29"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-flexibility-contract","v141-b-g02-p01"],"required_work":"Recheck the bounds, indices and per-contract metering convention of the relevant source equations, and clarify the relationship among demand quantity, energy per contract and bid units; retain the current frozen expression and case limitations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G012","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Standardized contracts, individual utility selection, stable results, iterative negotiation, aggregator intermediation and verification of full substitutability are still carried by coarse-grained nodes. The related proposals remain unapproved and must not be regarded as newly added ontological objects because of this cluster's assembly.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Ui","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C009","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g03-E01"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-flexibility-contract","v141-b-g02-p01","proposal:v141-b-g01-agent-utility-choice","proposal:v141-b-g01-stable-outcome","proposal:v141-b-g01-iterative-price-negotiation","proposal:v141-b-g01-aggregator-intermediary","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually review each proposal and the applicable scope of existing nodes separately; if extension is needed, handle it through subsequent upstream versions, and this round retains only the proposal references."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G013","category":"unverified_source","description":"All new interfaces and object mappings in this cluster are based on unreviewed excerpts permitted by the experiment. The current B status remains unverified, and the attached C2 content does not mean that this experiment has completed independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the sources, mathematical object types and scope conditions of all chains and connections; assess the degree of candidate closure only after source verification and upstream gap handling are completed."}]},"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R002","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R005","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-10be07664c6496b7","COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","COMP-535650ecb2e046e9","COMP-75186ff50e007d27","COMP-b249861ac893186a"]});
